      "text": "To find the largest common divisor (also known as the greatest common divisor or GCD) of 342 and 285, we can use the Euclidean algorithm, which involves repeated division until we reach the remainder of 0. Here are the steps:\n\n1. **Divide 342 by 285**:\n   \\[\n   342 \\div 285 \\approx 1.22037\n   \\]\n   So, we take the integer part, which is 1.\n\n2. **Find the remainder**:\n   \\[\n   342 - 1 \\times 285 = 342 - 285 = 57\n   \\]\n   Therefore, \\( 342 = 1 \\times 285 + 57 \\).\n\n3. **Update the values**:\n   Now, replace 285 with 57, and 342 with 1. Compute \\( \\frac{57}{1} \\):\n   \\[\n   57 \\div 1 = 57\n   \\]\n   Thus, the integer part of the division is 57.\n\n4. **Find the remainder**:\n   \\[\n   57 - 1 \\times 57 = 57 - 57 = 0\n   \\]\n\nAt this step, the remainder is 0, and no further divisions are necessary. This means 1 is the GCD of 342 and 285.\n\nThe final conclusion is that the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285 is \\boxed{57}.",
