    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285, we need to find the highest common divisor (HCD) of the two numbers. We can do this by finding the prime factorization of both 342 and 285 and then finding the product of the common factors.\n\nPrime factorization of 342:\n- 2 is a factor of 342 (assume 342/2=171)\n- 3 is a factor of 171 (assume 171/3=57)\n- 3 is a factor of 57 (assume 57/3=19)\n- 19 is a prime number, a factor of only itself\n\nPrime factorization of 285:\n- 3 is a prime factor, a factor of only itself (285/3=95)\n- 5 is a factor of 95 (assume 95/5=19)\n\nNow we have the prime factorizations:\n342 = 2*3*3*3*19\n285 = 3*5*19\n\nNext, we find the common prime factors:\n\n[ Find common primes in both factorizations: 3 and 19 ]\n342: 2*3*3*3*19 and 285: 3*3*19\n\nList out the remaining unique prime factors of both numbers filled in:\n342: 2*3*3*3*19\n285: 3*3*19\n\nThe HCD can be revised, utilizing the common prime factors 2, 3, and 19, finding their lowest powers:\n2 * 3^1 * 19^1 = 2*3*19 = 114\n\nSo, the largest factor common to both 342 and 285 is 114. The answer is: 114",
